{{Quote|There's an ocean planet&hellip; home to Nautolans. Glee Anselm?|Mace Windu|audio=HomeOfNautolans-CotF.flac|<ref name="Children of the Force" />}}
The '''Nautolans''' were a [[humanoid]] [[species]] from the [[planet]] [[Glee Anselm]]. They were [[Amphibian|amphibious]], and adapted to survive in harsh environments. Nautolan society was largely peaceful, but they were at odds with the [[Anselmi]], a related species also native to their home planet.

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|I'm Nautolan, a fact of which I'm sure you're both aware. Green skin, big black eyes, what else would I be? What you might not know is that these tentacles of mine let me pick up pheromones from other beings, which I translate into an understanding of their emotional states. That's how I know you two...are terrified.|[[Captain]] [[Finial Bright]], to [[Peeples]] and [[Innamin]]|<ref name="Light of the Jedi">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref>}}
[[File:ZattFull-CGSWG.png|thumb|left|200px|Zatt, a male Nautolan youngling]]
Nautolans were [[Amphibian|amphibious]], capable of breathing both air and water.<ref name="Nautolan" /> They were known to be capable of surviving in extreme environments.<ref name="Mace Windu 1">[[Jedi of the Republic – Mace Windu 1|''Jedi of the Republic – Mace Windu'' 1]]</ref> Their skin could be [[Color|green]], blue, gray,<ref name="Myths and Fables">{{StoryCite|story=Vengeful Waves|book=Myths & Fables}}</ref> purple,<ref name="Monster" /> orange,<ref name="Vader 11" /> or yellow,<ref name="Children of the Force" /> with red or green blood.<ref name="Path of Deceit">''[[The High Republic: Path of Deceit]]''</ref> One of their most notable features were their large, dark [[eye]]s,<ref name="Bounty Hunters 2" /> which were a product of evolution; through these eyes, they could spot details in lightless [[ocean]]s.<ref name="Light of the Jedi" />

Another notable detail were their long tendrils, which grew from their heads.<ref name="Bounty Hunters 2" /> These tendrils contained highly-sensitive olfactory receptors that were chemical-sensing,<ref name="Kit Fisto Base 1">{{SWCT|set=Base Series 1|cardname=Kit Fisto - Galactic Republic}}</ref> and most notably used to detect pheromones,<ref name="Bounty Hunters 2" /> allowing them to perceive expressions of emotion and other subtle changes in the body.<ref name="Kit Fisto Base 1" /> Nautolans could translate pheromones emitted by other beings into an understanding of a being's emotional state.<ref name="Light of the Jedi" /> These head tresses could be severed, and were incapable of growing back.<ref name="Path of Deceit" />

==Society and culture==
[[File:ConvertingShips-FO.png|thumb|right|212px|A Nautolan technician working a speeder]]
The Nautolans were known as a peaceful race, and disliked unnecessary violence. However, when forced to fight, they were skilled warriors. They had great respect for what they called the "ocean spirit," which they believed existed to maintain the balance of nature on Glee Anselm. Nautolan society was prosperous, and they were generous in sharing their resources with others.<ref name="Myths and Fables" /> The species was most comfortable underwater, preferring to be immersed in liquid.<ref name="VE" />

The Nautolan language, [[Nautila]], involved the use of pheromones to communicate. These pheromones could be used to convey complex ideas, including full sentences and map coordinates.<ref name="Bounty Hunters 2" /> Nautolans had a cultural tradition moving their faces close together, placing one's cheeks next to another's cheeks, when saying goodbye.<ref name="Path of Deceit" />

==History==
===Myth and legend===
[[File:VengefulWaves.jpg|thumb|left|190px|Legend held that the Anselmi empire was destroyed by a storm after they ignored the Nautolans' warnings about upsetting the balance of nature.]]
According to legend, the Nautolans lived underwater on their home planet of Glee Anselm, with the first members of their species living simply in caves until, over thousands of years, their society spread to encompass large areas of the ocean floor. At first, the Nautolans coexisted peacefully with their neighbors, the Anselmi, but after some time the Anselmi grew jealous of the Nautolans and began to threaten them and encroach upon their territory. In response to this, the [[Nautolan monarchy|Queen of the Nautolans]] warned the Anselmi that their actions would anger the spirit of the ocean. The Anselmi recognized that continuing to threaten the Nautolans could lead to war, and so they moved out of Glee Anselm's ocean and onto a large landmass.<ref name="Myths and Fables" />

The Nautolans continued to send [[ambassador]]s to the Anselmi, warning them against upsetting the balance of nature, but their representatives were consistently sent away. Eventually, the Anselmi's desire to expand led them to build massive [[dam]]s to hold back the ocean itself. In the end, that angered the ocean spirit so much that it brought down a storm to destroy the Anselmi empire and submerge it beneath the water. The Nautolans mourned that the Anselmi had not listened to their warnings, and continued to live peacefully, keeping in mind the importance of the natural balance.<ref name="Myths and Fables" /> Unable to breath underwater, the Anselmi were forced to make due on the little land available on Glee Anselm.<ref name="Choose Your Destiny" />

===Across the stars===
Having gone beyond their homeworld by the [[High Republic Era]],<ref name="Path of Deceit" /> Nautolans could be found in many places in the [[galaxy]].<ref name="Choose Your Destiny">''[[Choose Your Destiny: An Obi-Wan & Anakin Adventure]]''</ref> In the late [[Republic Era]],<ref name="Jango Fett 3">[[Jango Fett 3|''Jango Fett'' 3]]</ref> Anselmi extremists attacked the Nautolans.<ref name="Bounty Hunters 5">[[Bounty Hunters 5|''Bounty Hunters'' 5]]</ref> Eventually, a [[Anselmi–Nautolan war|war]] was waged between the Anselmi and Nautolans that the [[Galactic Republic]] hoped to put a stop to,<ref name="Jango Fett 1">[[Jango Fett 1|''Jango Fett'' 1]]</ref> but those efforts failed thanks to the efforts of [[Count]] [[Dooku]], and the conflict resumed.<ref name="Jango Fett 4">[[Jango Fett 4|''Jango Fett'' 4]]</ref> In [[26 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines Anakin">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[Choose Your Destiny: An Obi-Wan & Anakin Adventure]]'' to [[26 BBY]].</ref> a grouping of Anselm, who referred to the Nautolans as "gill heads," swore that one day they would dominate them.<ref name="Choose Your Destiny" />

==Nautolans in the galaxy==
[[File:Force_crush_KoF.png|thumb|right|190px|A Nautolan Force-user crushes a [[IG-100 MagnaGuard|MagnaGuard]].]]
The Nautolan [[Werth Plouth]] was a leader of the [[Path of the Open Hand]] [[Religion|cult]] on the planet [[Dalna]] under the title of "the [[Herald (title)|Herald]]." In the cult, he was joined by his wife, [[Opari Plouth]], and daughter, [[Kor Plouth]], both of whom were also Nautolans. The Herald had a distinctive appearance in part due to his cut head tendrils. After "[[Elecia Zeveron|the Mother]]" arrived on Dalna, she would assume control of the cult from Plouth. After the Mother arranged the death of Kor and other Path operatives, the Herald entered into a power struggle against the Mother with the aid of his daughter's [[Evereni]] girlfriend, [[Yana Ro]].<ref name="Path of Deceit" /> In the end, however, the Herald and Mother would lose control to Yana's cousin [[Marda Ro]], with both the Herald and the Mother quickly adapting to join Marda's [[Path of the Closed Fist]].<ref name="Path of Ven">''[[The High Republic: Path of Vengeance]]''</ref>

During the High Republic, the Nautolan named [[Rix Tegano]] taught [[Jedi Initiate]]s [[sky skimming]] lessons on the planet of [[Kondoraan]].<ref name="The Great Leaf Glide">''{{YJA|The Great Leaf Glide}}''</ref>  [[Argomon]] was a black marker smuggler.<ref name="THRA 3">[[The High Republic Adventures (2023) 3|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2023) 3]]</ref> A number of Nautolans were members of the [[Jedi Order]], including Palpatine's slain victim [[Jedi Master]] [[Kit Fisto]],<ref name="AOTC">{{Film|II}}</ref> the [[Padawan]] [[Knox]],<ref name="Monster" /> and the [[youngling]] [[Zatt]].<ref name="The Gathering" /> The [[Trident-class assault ship|''Trident''-class assault ship]] ''[[Nautolan's Revenge]]'' shared its name with the species.<ref name="Armada coming soon">{{Twitter|atomicmassgames|status/1398368654073413635|Atomic Mass Games|quote=Two new options for Scum and Villainy and a new title also usable by the Separatist Alliance add evocative options to the Trident-class Assault Ship. How will you use these new upgrades to further your treacherous, tabletop agenda? #StarWars #StarWarsXwing #Xwing #miniatures|archivedate=20210528201727}}</ref>

[[Nakano Lash]] was a prominent Nautolan [[bounty hunter]], working alongside the likes of [[Boba Fett]] and [[Bossk'wassak'Cradossk|Bossk]].<ref name="Bounty Hunters 1">[[Bounty Hunters 1|''Bounty Hunters'' 1]]</ref> [[Fong Do]] was a male Nautolan bounty hunter who was close friends with [[Castas]].<ref name="LT">{{TCW|Lethal Trackdown}}</ref> A Nautolan fought alongside [[Cassian Jeron Andor]] in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]],<ref name="Adventures in Wookiee-Sitting">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=3|story=Tales from Wild Space: Adventures in Wookiee-Sitting}}</ref> and a Nautolan named [[Daz Crano]] piloted a [[T-70 X-wing starfighter]] for the [[Resistance]] during their [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] against the [[First Order]].<ref name="Star Wars Adventures 27">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=27|story=Ghosts of Kashyyyk, Part 1}}</ref>

[[Caij Vanda]] was a Nautolan bounty hunter who encountered [[Cal Kestis]].<ref name="Survivor">''[[Star Wars Jedi: Survivor]]''</ref>

